================================================================================
SECTION 1 — CDI (Containerized Data Importer)
================================================================================

CDI-01 [C] Import hung despite API=Running
  Signal : rate(bytes transferred by importer pod) flat for >5 min while
           DataVolume phase=ImportInProgress; use deriv() on network bytes
           for the importer pod namespace
  Playbook: Restart importer pod; verify source URL reachability; inspect
            scratch PVC usage; escalate to storage if NFS/S3 unreachable

CDI-02 [C] DataVolume stuck in Pending
  Signal : kube_persistentvolumeclaim_status_phase{phase="Pending"} for
           CDI-owned PVCs > 10 minutes
  Playbook: Check StorageClass provisioner pod health; verify SC exists and
            is default; check node disk pressure

CDI-03 [B] Importer pod CrashLoopBackOff
  Signal : kube_pod_container_status_restarts_total{pod=~"importer-.*"} > 3
           in 10m  (built-in: CDIDataVolumeUnusualRestartCount)
  Playbook: Pull importer logs; validate registry credentials; check scratch
            PVC space; verify proxy/NetworkPolicy config

CDI-04 [C] Import duration exceeds SLA
  Signal : Custom: track DV creation timestamp vs rolling p95 historical
           duration; deriv(bytes_transferred) below expected rate
  Playbook: Notify requester; check node disk I/O contention; check source
            bandwidth

CDI-05 [C] Scratch PVC space exhausted
  Signal : kubelet_volume_stats_used_bytes / kubelet_volume_stats_capacity_bytes
           {namespace="cdi"} > 0.9
  Playbook: Auto-expand scratch PVC if SC supports it; clean orphaned scratch
            PVCs; alert storage admin

CDI-06 [B] CDI operator degraded
  Signal : csv_succeeded{name=~"cdi-operator.*"}==0 or
           cluster_operator_conditions{condition="Degraded"}==1
           (built-in: CDIOperatorDown)
  Playbook: Check cdi-operator pod logs; reconcile CRs; check OLM subscription

CDI-07 [E] Registry/HTTP source unreachable
  Signal : K8s Event reason=ImportFailed with connection-refused pattern
           via Splunk event pipeline
  Playbook: Validate source URL; check NetworkPolicy; verify pull secret;
            test proxy config

================================================================================
SECTION 2 — KubeVirt / virt-launcher
================================================================================

KV-01 [B] VM stuck in Starting phase
  Signal : kubevirt_vmi_phase_count{phase="Pending"} duration > 10m
           (built-in: KubeVirtVMStuck)
  Playbook: Check node resource availability; verify device plugin VF
            allocation; check image pull; inspect virt-launcher logs

KV-02 [C] Live migration hung
  Signal : deriv(kubevirt_vmi_migration_data_remaining_bytes[5m]) >= 0
           while migration phase=Migrating; also check
           kubevirt_vmi_migration_phase_transition_time_seconds vs baseline
  Playbook: Abort via virtctl; check target node resources; verify
            live-migration network bandwidth; review bandwidthPerMigration

KV-03 [B] Migration repeated failures
  Signal : increase(kubevirt_vmi_migration_failed_total[1h]) > 3
           (built-in: KubeVirtVMIExcessiveMigrations)
  Playbook: Check live-migration network (Multus/SR-IOV); check target node
            resources; temporarily disable migration; review evictionStrategy

KV-04 [B] VMI unexpected crash/restart
  Signal : kubevirt_vmi_phase_count{phase="Failed"} increase; also
           kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason for virt-launcher
  Playbook: Pull guest serial console logs; check host node health; inspect
            qemu crash dump; notify VM owner

KV-05 [C] virt-launcher OOMKilled
  Signal : kube_pod_container_status_last_terminated_reason="OOMKilled"
           for virt-launcher pods
  Playbook: Adjust VM memory requests/limits; review cluster overcommit ratio;
            migrate VM to larger node

KV-06 [C] High guest memory swap-in
  Signal : rate(kubevirt_vmi_memory_swap_in_traffic_bytes_total[5m])
           above established baseline
  Playbook: Alert VM owner to resize; check node memory pressure; tune
            balloon driver

KV-07 [C] Guest agent not responding
  Signal : kubevirt_vmi_info{guest_os_info} absent or
           last_api_connection_timestamp_seconds stale > 5m
  Playbook: Attempt virtctl guestosinfo; SSH into VM; reinstall qemu-guest-agent;
            escalate to VM owner

KV-08 [C] Live migration network saturated
  Signal : node_network_transmit_bytes_total on migration NIC near wire rate;
           compare to kubevirt migration bandwidth limit config
  Playbook: Throttle other workloads on node; reduce bandwidthPerMigration;
            schedule migration off-peak

KV-09 [C] vCPU steal time high
  Signal : rate(kubevirt_vmi_vcpu_seconds{state="steal"}[5m]) > threshold
  Playbook: Cordon node; redistribute VMs; review CPU overcommit ratio

KV-10 [E] VM disk hotplug failure
  Signal : K8s Event reason=HotplugVolumeMount failure via Splunk;
           also CSI attacher error events
  Playbook: Check CSI node plugin on target node; retry hotplug; verify
            PVC RWO/RWX mode compatibility

