SECTION 6 — HashiCorp Vault
================================================================================

VLT-01 [C] Vault sealed
  Signal : vault_core_unsealed==0 (vault-exporter sidecar) or
           Vault health endpoint returning 503 via blackbox prober
  Playbook: Trigger auto-unseal (HSM/KMS); if manual — page on-call, run
            unseal with quorum of key shares; check audit log for cause

VLT-02 [C] Vault raft leader election failure
  Signal : vault_raft_leader_lastContact_seconds > threshold or
           vault_core_leadership_lost_count increasing
  Playbook: Check raft peer connectivity; verify Vault pods reach each other;
            restart follower nodes one at a time

VLT-03 [C] Token/lease TTL storm
  Signal : vault_token_count_by_ttl spike;
           vault_core_handle_request_blocked high
  Playbook: Identify noisy client via audit log; revoke orphaned tokens;
            increase batch-token usage; add rate-limit policy

VLT-04 [C] Vault PKI-issued cert expiry
  Signal : Custom cert-expiry exporter scanning Vault PKI issued certs;
           ssl_certificate_expiry_seconds < 7d
  Playbook: Trigger cert-manager renewal referencing Vault issuer; alert
            service owner; verify auto-rotation job health

VLT-05 [E] Vault agent sidecar injection failure
  Signal : K8s Event for init container failure on vault-agent-init via
           Splunk; also vault_agent_inject_errors counter
  Playbook: Check Vault agent injector pod; verify Vault policy allows SA;
            check NetworkPolicy between pod and Vault service

VLT-06 [C] Vault storage backend latency
  Signal : vault_core_backend_put_operations_duration_seconds p99 > threshold
  Playbook: Check underlying Vault PVC I/O; check Raft segment size; if on
            etcd backend check etcd health

VLT-07 [C] Vault audit log write failure
  Signal : vault_audit_log_request_failure increasing
  Playbook: Clear/rotate audit log backend; fix audit device connectivity;
            add secondary audit device for redundancy

