SECTION 9 — Storage (General OCP / VM Disks)
================================================================================

STR-01 [C] RWO PVC used for live-migration VM (pre-flight config alert)
  Signal : Custom static check: VMI evictionStrategy=LiveMigrate AND
           PVC accessMode=ReadWriteOnce — fire before migration is attempted
  Playbook: Change PVC access mode to RWX or change evictionStrategy to
            Evict; alert VM owner

STR-02 [B] Thin-pool storage near depletion
  Signal : ceph_pool_percent_used > 85 or
           lvm_lv_usage_bytes / lvm_lv_size_bytes > 0.85
           (built-in: CephPoolNearFull)
  Playbook: Expand pool proactively; set Ceph nearfull/backfillfull ratios;
            alert storage admin before VM disks become read-only

STR-03 [B] Ceph OSD down
  Signal : ceph_osd_up==0 (built-in: CephOSDDown)
  Playbook: Check OSD pod logs; check underlying disk health (smartctl);
            add replacement OSD; monitor rebalance progress

STR-04 [B] Ceph I/O latency spike
  Signal : ceph_osd_apply_latency_ms p99 > threshold
           (built-in: CephOSDSlowOps)
  Playbook: Identify noisy VM or volume; check network between OSDs; check
            OSD disk queue depth; apply hotspot mitigation

STR-05 [B] Persistent volume nearing full
  Signal : kubelet_volume_stats_used_bytes /
           kubelet_volume_stats_capacity_bytes > 0.9
           (built-in: KubePersistentVolumeFillingUp)
  Playbook: Alert VM owner; auto-expand if SC supports; run housekeeping
            inside guest; resize via virtctl

================================================================================
IMPLEMENTATION GUIDANCE
================================================================================

1. BUILT-IN ALERTS — wire to playbooks via Alertmanager routes
   Check existing rules first:
     oc get prometheusrules -n openshift-cnv -o yaml
     oc get prometheusrules -n openshift-storage -o yaml
     kubectl get prometheusrules -n kube-system -o yaml   # Portworx
   Add routes in Alertmanager config matching alertname and route to playbook
   webhook/PagerDuty/Opsgenie receiver.

2. CUSTOM ALERTS — write PrometheusRule CRs
   Key patterns:
   - Hung transfer: deriv(metric[5m]) < threshold while parent phase active
   - Duration vs baseline: compare to recording rule tracking p95 over 7d
   - Capacity: ratio of used/total > threshold with for: 5m
   - Cert expiry: time() - cert_not_after_timestamp < 7*24*3600

3. EVENT-STREAM ALERTS — K8s Events → Splunk
   Deploy event-exporter (e.g. kubernetes-event-exporter) to ship K8s
   Events to Splunk. Build Splunk alerts on:
   - reason field patterns (ImportFailed, FailedCreatePodSandBox,
     HotplugVolumeMount, etc.)
   - involvedObject.namespace + reason combinations
   Use Splunk alert actions to call Alertmanager API or ticketing system.

4. ALERT PRIORITY TIERS
   P1 (page immediately): VLT-01 (Vault sealed), PX-05 (quorum lost),
      OCP-01 (node NotReady+VMs), KV-03 (migration failure loop),
      STR-03 (OSD down)
   P2 (alert + auto-remediate): CDI-01 (hung import), KV-02 (hung migration),
      PX-01 (StorageDown), CSM-03 (array connectivity), OCP-03 (etcd latency)
   P3 (ticket + monitor): CDI-04 (SLA breach), KV-06 (swap-in), NET-01 (VF
      exhaustion), VLT-03 (token storm), CSM-05 (RPO breach)
   P4 (informational/pre-flight): STR-01 (RWO+LiveMigrate config mismatch),
      KCP-04 (cert expiry warning), OCP-05 (HugePages low)

5. EXPORTERS NEEDED (if not already deployed)
   - vault-exporter or vault-agent with prometheus telemetry (Vault metrics)
   - node-exporter (standard; HugePages, network, disk metrics)
   - blackbox-exporter (Vault health endpoint, array management IPs)
   - cert-exporter (webhook certs, PKI certs)
   - kubernetes-event-exporter (K8s Events → Splunk)
   - CSM metrics endpoint (check CSM operator docs for scrape config)
   - SR-IOV device plugin metrics endpoint

